course: dictionary
lesson: 11821
title: Bionic: two words in one
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from two smaller words joined together. Knowing the parts can help you guess the meaning. «Bionic» mixes «biology», the study of living things, and «electronic», which means powered by tiny electrical parts. Put them together and you get a body part that is part living, part machine.
explain: «Mia's new bionic hand lets her pick up an egg without breaking it.» The clues are new hand and pick up. A bionic hand must be a hand that works like a real one, and the sentence says it works well. Swap in your meaning: "Mia's new hand with electronic parts, which works like a real hand, lets her pick up an egg." It still makes sense.
explain: The word is also used informally, in stories and on TV. «The bionic hero ran faster than the racing car.» Here bionic does not mean a real machine part. It means super-strong or with powers beyond normal. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Bionic means having body parts that are electronic or mechanical and work like real ones.
fact: Bionic body parts are often better than the real ones they work like.
fact: Bionic arms, hands and eyes can help people who have lost a limb or their sight.
fact: Informally, bionic means super-strong or with powers beyond normal, as in stories and TV.
fact: «Bionic» mixes «biology» and «electronic».
exercise: «Mia's new bionic hand lets her pick up an egg without breaking it.» What does bionic mean here? | *A hand with electronic or mechanical parts that works like a real one | A hand made of wood | A hand that can only wave | A hand that is always cold
exercise: «The bionic hero ran faster than the racing car.» What does bionic suggest in this sentence? | *Super-strong, with powers beyond normal | Made of paper | Ill and tired | Lost in a race
exercise: Which two words is bionic built from? | bison and tonic | *biology and electronic | bird and tractor | bicycle and tonic
test: Which of these could be a bionic body part? | *A bionic eye that helps a person see | A pair of socks | A bowl of soup | A pencil
test: Why do bionic arms and hands help people? | They stop people from feeling cold | *They help people who have lost a limb | They make people taller | To make tea faster for everyone
exam: «The bionic knee helped Grandad walk to the shops.» What is the best meaning of bionic in this sentence? | *An electronic or mechanical knee that works like a real one | Made of biscuits | A knee painted gold | A knee that is sore
